# WordPress Content Editing

Use this Rule when editing WordPress page content through REST, MCP, or WP-CLI in a project that uses ACF Flexible Content.

## Core Model

ACF Flexible Content stores page sections as an ordered array. Each item has an `acf_fc_layout` value that identifies the layout type. The available layout names, page IDs, field keys, and clone group keys belong in project context.

## Read Before Writing

Before changing content:

1. Read the page or post including its ACF data.
2. Identify the target block by page ID, array index, layout name, visible content, or Section handoff.
3. Preserve the full Flexible Content array.
4. Change only the fields requested by the task.
5. Verify the resulting content on the target URL.

## Write The Complete Array

When updating a page through REST, send the complete `flexible_content` array back. Do not send only the changed block.

Generic REST shape:

```http
POST /wp-json/wp/v2/pages/<page-id>
```

```json
{
  "acf": {
    "flexible_content": []
  }
}
```

Populate the array from the read response, then apply the intended minimal edit.

## Fields To Preserve

Do not change these unless the user explicitly asks:

- `acf_fc_layout`
- ACFE layout metadata fields.
- Layout/style fields.
- Image and media attachment IDs.
- Button link targets, variants, and IDs.
- Nested Flexible Content structure.

Nested Flexible Content blocks follow the same rule: preserve the full nested array and edit only the intended fields.

## Type Normalization

REST reads may return values in a shape that differs from what writes accept. Before writing:

- Convert ACFE toggle booleans to the value shape accepted by the project.
- Keep enum fields on valid project-defined values.
- Use attachment IDs for media fields, not URLs.
- Preserve existing HTML patterns in rich text fields.

## Handoff Notes

If content edits affect a Section that will receive local frontend work, update the Section handoff with:

- Page URL.
- Changed content fields.
- Any layout/style fields deliberately preserved.
- Any visual behavior that still needs CSS or Playwright verification.
